<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Inverse Trigonometric Functions — solving sin^-1(x) = theta for x</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Suppose \( \sin^{-1}(x) = {@thetadeg@}^\circ \). This angle lies in the principal range \([-90^\circ, 90^\circ]\) of \(\sin^{-1}\).</p>
<p>Find the exact value of \(x\). Type \(\sqrt{2}\) as <code>sqrt(2)</code>.</p>
<div>\(x = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\sin^{-1}(x) = \theta\) means exactly the same as \(x = \sin\theta\), with \(\theta\) in the principal range. The inverse function undoes sine, so to find \(x\) apply \(\sin\) to both sides:</p>
\[ x = \sin({@thetadeg@}^\circ) = {@ta@}. \]
<p>The unknown \(x\) is a ratio (a number between \(-1\) and \(1\)), not an angle. [[if test="is(thetadeg<0)"]]Since sine is an odd function, \(\sin({@thetadeg@}^\circ) = -\sin({@-thetadeg@}^\circ)\), which is negative.[[/if]]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text>basedeg: rand([30,45,60]);
thetadeg: rand([-1,1])*basedeg;
/* exact value from Maxima, checked for all six angles */
ta: sin(thetadeg*%pi/180);
/* Diagnostics (all distinct from ta and from each other):
   x taken as the angle in degrees; x taken as the angle in radians; sign error */
wrong_angle: thetadeg;
wrong_angle_rad: thetadeg*%pi/180;
wrong_sign: -ta;</text>
    </questionvariables>
    <specificfeedback format="html">
